  "description": "Accounting cannot reach the server. Everything looks configured.",
  "brief": "🚨 NETWORK OUTAGE\n\nThe accounting department reports that the server is unreachable. PC-01 and PC-02 can still ping each other, so the local network is fine. Every machine has an address, a mask and a gateway filled in.\n\nOne of those values sends packets somewhere that does not exist. Find it.",
  "hints": [
    "PC-01 and PC-02 can reach each other — so the switch and cabling are fine.",
    "Compare 'ipconfig' on PC-01 with 'ipconfig' on PC-02, line by line.",
    "Then check which address Router-01 actually has on that subnet.",
    "A gateway that nobody answers for is as bad as no gateway at all."
